1
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:03,380
♪

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,350
[SITARA (ADULT)]
In the distant past,

3
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:10,480
scholars used geometry
to establish the size

4
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:12,890
and scope of Earth
for the first time.

5
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:15,770
In which case,

6
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:19,320
could one also use geometry
to determine the size and scope

7
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:21,860
of the fate we hold
in our very hands?

8
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:25,660
This is the story of a witch
who made a vast,

9
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,950
expansive continent
into her plaything.

10
00:00:28,990 --> 00:00:31,450
♪

11
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:48,890
[Sitara pants]

12
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:52,600
[Ahmad groans]

13
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:57,310
[Muslim prayer call
in the distance]

14
00:01:18,710 --> 00:01:20,550
[Ahmad gasps, grunts]

15
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:22,460
[Sitara
continues panting]

16
00:01:27,010 --> 00:01:28,260
[Pigeons cooing]

17
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:30,430
[Sitara gasps]

18
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:34,020
[Muslim prayer call
continues]

19
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,020
[gasps]

20
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:46,110
[AHMAD] Where are you trying
to fly to, my little bird?

21
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:47,530
[exclaims]

22
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:50,660
You're quite a handful, child!

23
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:58,120
♪

24
00:02:05,050 --> 00:02:06,720
[indistinct chatter]

25
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,050
♪

26
00:02:25,490 --> 00:02:27,190
I love the bazaar here.

27
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,150
It is so full of life.

28
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,200
Mistress, once your iddah

29
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,660
for the late master is over,
we'll go to the shops.

30
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:35,450
Yes, let's.

31
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,870
But today, I just hope
Allah will guide the way

32
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:39,870
and lead us
to find a fine slave.

33
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:41,880
-Uh?
-Not as fine as you, though.

34
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:43,630
[Fatima and Zumurrud laugh]

35
00:02:43,670 --> 00:02:45,210
[indistinct chatter]

36
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:49,880
[FATIMA] Hmm...

37
00:02:49,930 --> 00:02:52,180
Each one of them
is a hard worker.

38
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:53,430
[FATIMA] Hm.

39
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:56,020
This woman can cook up any meal
you desire,

40
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:57,270
for example.

41
00:02:57,350 --> 00:02:58,980
-She's a great seamstress.
-Hm. Hm.

42
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:01,520
And this one here
has the gift of gab.

43
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,980
What a perfect
conversation partner, right?

44
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:05,230
Well, perhaps.

45
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:07,780
But what we need help
with the most right now is...

46
00:03:07,820 --> 00:03:08,820
Is housecleaning.

47
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:09,860
That huge mansion

48
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:11,450
is just too much
for me to handle!

49
00:03:11,490 --> 00:03:14,370
Indeed, and I still haven't
finished sorting

50
00:03:14,410 --> 00:03:16,080
all my late husband's
belongings.

51
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,290
[AHMAD] Ah, say no more!

52
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:19,790
What do you think
about this woman, then?

53
00:03:19,830 --> 00:03:22,210
There's no one can clean
the way she does!

54
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:24,290
Hello, my name is Anis!

55
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,710
Cleaning isn't about
what you feel like discarding,

56
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:28,010
but what you wish to keep!

57
00:03:28,630 --> 00:03:31,380
Your days will be neat and tidy,
I give you my word!

58
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:34,050
That is wonderful!
How much would she be?

59
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:37,260
I'll let you have her
for 800 dirham.

60
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:40,600
[gasps] I know that slaves
are expensive, but my goodness.

61
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,350
Oh, please, Mr. Ahmad!

62
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,270
Isn't there any way
you could go lower?

63
00:03:44,810 --> 00:03:46,110
[AHMAD] Mmm...

64
00:03:46,150 --> 00:03:48,990
Normally, I would refuse
a request like that.

65
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:50,940
Just this one time, though.

66
00:03:50,990 --> 00:03:53,070
I will let you have her
for only half price!

67
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:54,120
[Fatima and Zumurrud gasp]

68
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:57,200
But in return for this...
Come here.

69
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,580
[FATIMA AND ZUMURRUD] Huh?

70
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:01,750
[SITARA] Uh?

71
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:08,250
[AHMAD] Now go on.
Do as I taught you.

72
00:04:08,670 --> 00:04:09,920
[Sitara chuckles]

73
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:11,340
Oh, how cute!

74
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:12,470
And who is she?

75
00:04:12,550 --> 00:04:15,390
Her name's Sitara,
and I just acquired her.

76
00:04:15,430 --> 00:04:17,970
Oh, your name's
meaning is "star."

77
00:04:18,010 --> 00:04:20,350
-That's so lovely!
-[Sitara chuckles]

78
00:04:20,390 --> 00:04:22,100
[Ahmad clears throat]

79
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:25,310
Although she may just be
a little bashful,

80
00:04:25,350 --> 00:04:27,730
her smile is quite fetching,
as you can see!

81
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:30,190
And if she were given
a proper education,

82
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:33,450
I think she could be a servant
to someone of high standing!

83
00:04:33,490 --> 00:04:35,200
So, here's what I'm proposing.

84
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,910
-Lady Fatima...
-[FATIMA] Uh?

85
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:39,950
Your household is known
for being rather scholarly,

86
00:04:39,990 --> 00:04:42,200
and Young Master Muhammad's
perceptive mind

87
00:04:42,250 --> 00:04:44,080
shines brightly
even here in Tus.

88
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:46,960
So, studying with you
will give her real cachet!

89
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,840
Might I trouble you to take her
into your home for a while?

90
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,380
[FATIMA AND ZUMURRUD] Huh?

91
00:04:56,090 --> 00:04:57,550
-[UNCLE] What?
-[SITARA] Uh?

92
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,640
You agreed to this?

93
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:01,180
Oh, please.

94
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:03,310
You're the only one
who's truly qualified

95
00:05:03,350 --> 00:05:05,100
to give her lessons now,
brother.

96
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:06,850
I'm still fulfilling my iddah,

97
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:08,560
and you're
the best teacher I know.

98
00:05:08,610 --> 00:05:11,650
As you are aware,
whether you're a slave or not,

99
00:05:11,690 --> 00:05:14,990
every Muslim's duty
is to seek knowledge.

100
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:17,530
I suppose.

101
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:19,030
[Sitara chuckles]

102
00:05:19,070 --> 00:05:21,910
Recitation's the cornerstone
of learning.

103
00:05:21,950 --> 00:05:23,700
And the first step
on that journey

104
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:25,250
is to recite the Quran
properly.

105
00:05:25,290 --> 00:05:27,250
So now I want you
to repeat after me.

106
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:28,290
[SITARA] Hm?

107
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:30,460
"In the mighty name of Allah,

108
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:33,800
the Most Gracious,
and also the Most Merciful."

109
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:38,140
Uh? Now it is your turn.

110
00:05:38,180 --> 00:05:39,340
[SITARA] Hmm?

111
00:05:39,390 --> 00:05:42,220
[UNCLE] Hmm? Well, go on.
Your turn.

112
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,890
[Sitara chuckles]

113
00:05:43,930 --> 00:05:44,980
♪

114
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:45,980
[bird chirping]

115
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:47,190
It's hopeless.

116
00:05:47,310 --> 00:05:50,150
No matter how hard I try,
she sits and smiles,

117
00:05:50,190 --> 00:05:52,730
showing absolutely no interest
in learning at all.

118
00:05:52,770 --> 00:05:54,860
But I swore I'd take her in.

119
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,070
[Sitara chuckles]

120
00:05:56,110 --> 00:05:58,110
You can keep the other slave.

121
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:59,570
I'll repay the discount.

122
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:01,660
I hope you'll forgive me,
brother.

123
00:06:01,990 --> 00:06:03,080
[Uncle sighs]

124
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,210
-[SITARA] Hmm?
-I'll have him come get you.

125
00:06:06,250 --> 00:06:08,040
-Just wait here, all right?
-[SITARA] Hm. Hm.

126
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:11,670
[UNCLE] No, I'll go.
Mr. Ahmad's establishment, yes?

127
00:06:11,710 --> 00:06:13,550
[FATIMA] Yes. I'm so sorry.

128
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,760
[SITARA]
Here's my chance!

129
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:24,930
If I don't leave, who knows
where I'll get sold off to?

130
00:06:24,970 --> 00:06:26,640
I need to go home!

131
00:06:26,730 --> 00:06:28,730
♪

132
00:06:36,190 --> 00:06:38,650
[man grunts]

133
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:44,040
[Sitara gasps]

134
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:46,080
[Zumurrud humming]

135
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,420
Find her?

136
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:52,580
[ZUMURRUD] Mm-mm.

137
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:54,670
[Uncle sighs]

138
00:06:58,380 --> 00:07:00,880
[Sitara gasps]
I'm so lost!

139
00:07:00,930 --> 00:07:02,470
How do I get out of here?

140
00:07:09,350 --> 00:07:11,270
[SITARA]
Can't let him see me.

141
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,440
[Sitara gasps]

142
00:07:19,650 --> 00:07:22,370
And Young Master Muhammad's
perceptive mind

143
00:07:22,410 --> 00:07:24,660
shines brightly
even here in Tus.

144
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:27,410
[MUHAMMAD] Uh?

145
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,330
[SITARA] Excuse me.

146
00:07:29,370 --> 00:07:30,580
Uh, where is the door?

147
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:32,830
Hey! This is most improper!

148
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:35,000
Don't you know that
a woman must not ever reveal

149
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,800
her uncovered hair to a man?

150
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:39,970
[chuckles] It's all right,
'cause I'm still little!

151
00:07:40,010 --> 00:07:41,260
You're too close.

152
00:07:41,590 --> 00:07:44,220
And besides, it looks to me
like you're still a child, too,

153
00:07:44,260 --> 00:07:45,680
Young Master Muhammad!

154
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:47,510
So, um, who are you?

155
00:07:47,930 --> 00:07:49,730
-My name is-- [gasps]
-[ZUMURRUD] Ah-ha!

156
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:51,020
Since you up and disappeared,

157
00:07:51,060 --> 00:07:52,940
I've been looking
all over the place for you!

158
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:56,230
Mm. The roses were so pretty,
I had to see them!

159
00:07:56,270 --> 00:07:58,280
Actually, she was looking
for the way out.

160
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,690
[Sitara grunts]

161
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:02,780
Unbelievable!

162
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:04,320
How could you try to escape?

163
00:08:04,370 --> 00:08:05,410
Now, now there.

164
00:08:05,450 --> 00:08:06,910
In only a few moments,

165
00:08:06,950 --> 00:08:09,120
my brother will be back here
with Mr. Ahmad.

166
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,160
I'm sorry.

167
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,210
Didn't you want to go back?

168
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:16,790
No, not back
to that man's place.

169
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:19,590
To the house where
my mother and I used to live.

170
00:08:20,090 --> 00:08:21,590
Soon after she died,

171
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:23,840
her master sold me off
to the highest bidder.

172
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:25,470
-[Fatima gasps]
-Then that isn't your house,

173
00:08:25,510 --> 00:08:26,470
so there's no point!

174
00:08:26,510 --> 00:08:28,310
Remember, you're a slave!

175
00:08:28,350 --> 00:08:30,430
If you want a real home
worth returning to,

176
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,930
study hard, so you'll be bought
by a good master!

177
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:34,810
No! I don't ever want to study!

178
00:08:34,850 --> 00:08:37,730
And I won't be making
cute faces anymore, either,

179
00:08:37,770 --> 00:08:40,490
because it only makes me seem
more valuable to them!

180
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,570
[cries] If I learn,
I'll just be sold again

181
00:08:42,610 --> 00:08:44,200
and taken away forever.

182
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:47,780
I'm sick of going places
where I don't recognize things!

183
00:08:47,830 --> 00:08:49,620
[cries]

184
00:08:50,410 --> 00:08:52,750
[MUHAMMAD] Little girl.
I mean, Sitara,

185
00:08:52,790 --> 00:08:55,000
is that the reason
you came here to study?

186
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,040
[SITARA] Uh?

187
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:59,500
Even though our lots in life
might seem fairly different...

188
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:00,840
Say, Zumurrud?

189
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:04,550
Will you go and fetch me
a water bucket from the kitchen?

190
00:09:04,590 --> 00:09:06,220
A large one please.

191
00:09:06,260 --> 00:09:07,680
[ZUMURRUD] Yes, of course.

192
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,930
[MUHAMMAD]
Come with me.

193
00:09:08,970 --> 00:09:10,260
[SITARA] Huh?

194
00:09:11,890 --> 00:09:13,640
Where are we going?

195
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,020
[Muhammad chuckles]

196
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:19,230
Up here?

197
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:28,320
Will this one here be all right?

198
00:09:28,370 --> 00:09:30,700
Mm-hmm. Thanks so much.

199
00:09:32,410 --> 00:09:34,870
I'll be dropping it
in the courtyard.

200
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:36,540
[BOTH] Huh?

201
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:40,420
[Muhammad grunting]

202
00:09:41,130 --> 00:09:42,340
Young master, why?

203
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:44,260
Do you really think
the girl is a lost cause?

204
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:45,670
-[loud clang]
-[both yelp]

205
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:48,510
[AHMAD] What on Earth was that?
Oh, my goodness!

206
00:09:48,550 --> 00:09:50,930
What's going on?

207
00:09:55,060 --> 00:09:56,600
[BOTH] Huh?

208
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:58,480
[UNCLE] Is everyone all right?
What was that?

209
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:00,480
Wait... Did lightning strike
the house?

210
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:03,070
Are... are you sure
those barbarous nomads

211
00:10:03,110 --> 00:10:05,650
haven't started attacking us?
[whimpers]

212
00:10:06,450 --> 00:10:07,650
[Uncle gasps]

213
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:09,700
-[Muhammad laughs]
-[UNCLE] A water bucket?

214
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:11,580
Everyone down there
was so afraid.

215
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:14,040
Young Master, your little prank
went too far!

216
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,790
Just out of curiosity,

217
00:10:15,830 --> 00:10:17,750
why are you two
so calm and composed?

218
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:19,500
Well, why wouldn't we be?

219
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:21,750
We knew you were
about to drop it,

220
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:23,460
and both of us covered our ears.

221
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,840
So what you're telling me is,

222
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:29,800
you both predicted
a future in which

223
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:31,180
there would be a loud noise,

224
00:10:31,220 --> 00:10:33,680
then you took some precautions.
That about right?

225
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:36,350
Well, yes. I suppose so.

226
00:10:37,430 --> 00:10:38,890
Then, just maybe

227
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:40,900
that's what
learning's all about.

228
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:42,400
[Sitara gasps softly]

229
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,610
[MUHAMMAD]
At the moment,

230
00:10:43,650 --> 00:10:45,820
you don't have
any idea where you are,

231
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:49,150
what's happening here,
or what is to become of you.

232
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:51,200
It's all so unknown.

233
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,080
My uncles
and the ones down there

234
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:54,700
are in a similar situation.

235
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:57,120
But if one were to study
and become wise,

236
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,210
then one would know
the best course of action,

237
00:10:59,250 --> 00:11:02,080
no matter what the situation
might be. Always.

238
00:11:02,630 --> 00:11:04,880
And that could never be
a bad thing.

239
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:07,470
Is that learning?

240
00:11:10,550 --> 00:11:13,100
-Uncle! I'm sorry about that!
-[ALL] Huh?

241
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:14,640
It was me!

242
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:17,520
[ANIS] Oh, this water bucket
is all bent now

243
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:19,020
and won't stack anymore!

244
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:20,680
How awful!

245
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:23,110
[ZUMURRUD] You can go
and have it repaired.

246
00:11:23,150 --> 00:11:25,190
I'll make sure
all the cooking is done.

247
00:11:25,270 --> 00:11:27,110
Ah! Hello there!

248
00:11:27,610 --> 00:11:28,780
[SITARA] Mm?

249
00:11:29,110 --> 00:11:31,900
If you ever have any questions,
feel free to ask me.

250
00:11:31,950 --> 00:11:33,030
[SITARA] I will.

251
00:11:33,950 --> 00:11:35,700
[SITARA (ADULT)]
With a new perspective.

252
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:38,830
Sitara remained
and found herself serving

253
00:11:38,870 --> 00:11:40,910
in a scholarly household.

254
00:11:42,210 --> 00:11:45,210
[Fatima humming]

255
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:48,690
[Sitara gasp excitedly]

256
00:12:48,730 --> 00:12:50,900
You're looking really beautiful,
Mistress!

257
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:52,400
Oh, thank you!

258
00:12:52,450 --> 00:12:54,490
Although, I feel rather
self-conscious.

259
00:12:54,530 --> 00:12:55,700
Now don't you be silly!

260
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:59,370
It's your first day going back
to the hammam after your iddah!

261
00:12:59,410 --> 00:13:01,830
So, go have some fun.
Put on a little makeup,

262
00:13:01,870 --> 00:13:03,540
dye your hair
and hands with henna,

263
00:13:03,580 --> 00:13:06,460
and start chatting up a storm
with all the other wives there!

264
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:08,170
Very well.

265
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:11,000
I'll bring you with me someday.

266
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:12,970
Sitara.

267
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:14,550
Great!

268
00:13:17,220 --> 00:13:20,430
"And to Allah belongs
all that is in the heavens,

269
00:13:20,470 --> 00:13:23,060
and all that is in the Earth."

270
00:13:24,310 --> 00:13:27,560
My recitation is still different
than Uncle's somehow.

271
00:13:27,610 --> 00:13:29,610
I should have him
teach me again.

272
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:31,610
[MUHAMMAD]
Mother, can we talk?

273
00:13:31,650 --> 00:13:33,570
[yelps] Uh, where is she?

274
00:13:33,610 --> 00:13:35,530
[SITARA] Mistress Fatima
left for the hammam

275
00:13:35,570 --> 00:13:37,070
a little while ago.

276
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:38,740
I thought she told you.

277
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:41,240
She did?
I forgot that was today.

278
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:43,450
Does this mean you only have
enough room up there

279
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:44,910
for your studies?

280
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,500
As I have told you before,

281
00:13:46,540 --> 00:13:48,960
please don't leave your room
with your hair uncovered.

282
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,170
And as I've told you,
I'm still a little girl!

283
00:13:52,550 --> 00:13:55,170
Besides, you're still only 12,
Young Master Muhammad.

284
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:58,260
What's so bad about somebody
who can't grow a beard

285
00:13:58,300 --> 00:14:00,180
setting foot in a girl's room?

286
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:02,100
I am not a child!

287
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:03,180
[Sitara laughs]

288
00:14:03,220 --> 00:14:05,140
Am I immature in your eyes
as well?

289
00:14:05,180 --> 00:14:06,180
[SITARA] Huh?

290
00:14:06,230 --> 00:14:07,390
[Muhammad sighs]

291
00:14:11,770 --> 00:14:13,570
[MUHAMMAD]
My teacher said I'm too ignorant

292
00:14:13,610 --> 00:14:15,400
in the ways of the world.

293
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:17,530
[SITARA] Do you mean
the one who teaches law?

294
00:14:17,570 --> 00:14:19,240
[MUHAMMAD]
Yes, Ustad Kamal al-Din,

295
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:22,240
whom Father introduced me to
before he died.

296
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:23,950
But recently though,

297
00:14:23,990 --> 00:14:27,120
I've sensed that we both have
very different views.

298
00:14:27,330 --> 00:14:29,000
He doesn't even give
clear answers

299
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:30,880
to certain questions
I pose to him.

300
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:33,170
You have
far too little experience

301
00:14:33,210 --> 00:14:35,420
to truly comprehend such things.

302
00:14:37,510 --> 00:14:40,720
That's why I'm leaving here
on a journey.

303
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:42,010
[Sitara gasps]

304
00:14:42,350 --> 00:14:45,560
I want to travel to Nishapur
and visit its renowned teachers.

305
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:49,390
But eventually, I'll explore
many other cities as well,

306
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:53,730
and engage with wisdom
from any and all sources...

307
00:14:54,230 --> 00:14:56,400
Searching for truth!

308
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:02,120
My father was a scholar,

309
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:04,660
and I believe that's the path
he wanted for me.

310
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:05,750
[Sitara exhales]

311
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:10,830
How wonderful!

312
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:13,790
Well, I have some washing to do,
so I need to go.

313
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:14,880
Sure.

314
00:15:18,130 --> 00:15:19,670
[SITARA]
"And to Allah belongs

315
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:22,850
all that is in the heavens
and all that is in the Earth."

316
00:15:25,970 --> 00:15:28,890
It seems like no matter
how hard I study,

317
00:15:28,930 --> 00:15:32,100
I'll never be able
to match Master Muhammad.

318
00:15:35,190 --> 00:15:38,240
[rooster crows]

319
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:43,490
♪

320
00:15:46,950 --> 00:15:48,700
Farewell, Mother.
I'm leaving now.

321
00:15:48,750 --> 00:15:51,500
To not bring shame
upon your dear father,

322
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:53,170
devote yourself to your studies.

323
00:15:53,210 --> 00:15:54,210
I will.

324
00:15:54,290 --> 00:15:56,590
Take good care of yourself.
[sniffles]

325
00:16:00,050 --> 00:16:02,130
As-salamu alaykum.

326
00:16:02,170 --> 00:16:04,220
[in English]
I will see you partway there.

327
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:06,050
Thank you for all this, Uncle.

328
00:16:06,430 --> 00:16:07,720
[gasps softly]

329
00:16:08,310 --> 00:16:09,520
Hold on.

330
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:10,680
Girl...

331
00:16:10,730 --> 00:16:11,770
[SITARA] Hmm?

332
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:13,770
So, I've been told
that you still can't read.

333
00:16:13,810 --> 00:16:14,980
No.

334
00:16:15,190 --> 00:16:16,440
-Well, then...
-Uh?

335
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:18,520
-I will be writing you letters.
-[gasps]

336
00:16:18,570 --> 00:16:20,240
So when I become a teacher,

337
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:21,950
I'll know how to convey
my lessons

338
00:16:21,990 --> 00:16:23,360
to young children like you.

339
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:25,070
And I'll write as simply
as I can.

340
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:27,160
-That good?
-I'm practice?

341
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,740
There is one thing I ask of you.

342
00:16:28,790 --> 00:16:30,790
Please study and read them
to Mother.

343
00:16:30,830 --> 00:16:32,500
Do you understand, Sitara?

344
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:33,790
[Sitara gasps]

345
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:36,290
No matter what, don't ever
stop learning, all right?

346
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:37,960
I won't. I promise.

347
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,380
And now I'm off.

348
00:16:46,470 --> 00:16:49,100
[SITARA (ADULT)] Muhammad,
a boy hailing from Tus,

349
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:51,560
who would become
a renowned scholar.

350
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:55,020
And Sitara,
a little slave girl...

351
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:56,860
This would be
the very last time

352
00:16:56,900 --> 00:17:00,190
they ever saw each other
face to face.

353
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:02,320
-[hooves clopping]
-[horse snorts]

354
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:05,450
[SITARA] "In the name of Allah,

355
00:17:05,490 --> 00:17:07,870
the Most Gracious,
the Most Merciful."

356
00:17:07,910 --> 00:17:09,160
Uh?

357
00:17:12,290 --> 00:17:14,000
[ZUMURRUD] It's the Tus militia.

358
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:15,540
Ms. Zumurrud?

359
00:17:15,580 --> 00:17:18,250
I bet they're on their way
to go scouting outside the city.

360
00:17:18,840 --> 00:17:20,170
From what I've been told,

361
00:17:20,210 --> 00:17:22,800
armed nomads have been
appearing in the area.

362
00:17:24,010 --> 00:17:26,590
My brother is down there
with them, somewhere.

363
00:17:26,630 --> 00:17:29,050
Though, I haven't seen him
in ages.

364
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:30,100
[SITARA] Huh?

365
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:31,390
Mikhail and I were born

366
00:17:31,430 --> 00:17:33,730
in a distant land
far to the west.

367
00:17:34,390 --> 00:17:36,640
Right on the sea!
And when the sun set,

368
00:17:36,690 --> 00:17:39,360
it turned everything
into a lovely purple!

369
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:40,480
[SITARA] Really?

370
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:41,650
We were both poor,

371
00:17:41,690 --> 00:17:44,490
but I still loved
watching the sea!

372
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:46,400
-[FATIMA] Sitara?
-[SITARA] Uh?

373
00:17:46,450 --> 00:17:48,700
Could I trouble you
to read this letter?

374
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:50,870
Yes! Of course!

375
00:17:50,910 --> 00:17:52,790
In the usual room, right?

376
00:17:52,830 --> 00:17:55,450
My goodness!
Look at how happy she is!

377
00:17:55,500 --> 00:17:56,750
[Fatima laughs]

378
00:17:57,330 --> 00:17:58,630
All right. So,

379
00:17:58,670 --> 00:18:02,250
"Mom, Uncle,
In these past eight years,

380
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:04,420
I've studied many fields
of learning,

381
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:07,430
including philosophy,
medicine, and astronomy.

382
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:09,090
[MUHAMMAD]
Nishapur is a sprawling,

383
00:18:09,130 --> 00:18:12,060
vibrant city where
many noted scholars gather.

384
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:15,600
For example, I was instructed
by Farid al-Din Damad

385
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:18,230
in the medical arts founded
by Ibn Sina.

386
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:20,060
Unlike theology,

387
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,690
in which one simply parrots
what one is taught,

388
00:18:22,730 --> 00:18:24,940
science is knowledge
that's built upon

389
00:18:24,980 --> 00:18:26,900
real-world experiences.

390
00:18:26,950 --> 00:18:28,700
[BOTH] I'm finding
this way of learning

391
00:18:28,740 --> 00:18:30,240
is far more agreeable.

392
00:18:30,570 --> 00:18:31,700
And also...

393
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:32,790
[chuckles]

394
00:18:32,990 --> 00:18:34,910
...if our little star, Sitara,
would be open

395
00:18:34,950 --> 00:18:36,200
to learning about them,

396
00:18:36,330 --> 00:18:38,660
please see that she studies
the various postulates

397
00:18:38,710 --> 00:18:40,960
and theorems
of Euclid and Ptolemy."

398
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,210
-Uh?
-[both chuckle]

399
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:45,550
Come along with me.

400
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:52,100
[Sitara exclaims]

401
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:55,140
Can't believe you're showing me
all of these precious books.

402
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:56,600
-Thanks!
-Of course.

403
00:18:56,770 --> 00:19:00,940
It's a duty upon each Muslim
to continue seeking knowledge.

404
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:03,900
That's what my late
scholar husband had told me.

405
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:06,690
"Euclid's Elements"
is that one right there.

406
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:08,240
Great!

407
00:19:08,780 --> 00:19:10,490
[grunts]

408
00:19:15,990 --> 00:19:18,830
It says, "A point is that
which has no part."

409
00:19:18,870 --> 00:19:20,920
And that "a line
is breadthless length."

410
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:23,670
Therefore, "The ends
of a line are points."

411
00:19:23,710 --> 00:19:25,800
It's like he's just stating
obvious things

412
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:27,800
in a really complicated way.

413
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:30,470
[FATIMA] But why do
obvious things seem so obvious?

414
00:19:30,510 --> 00:19:32,850
It's through amassing examples
one by one

415
00:19:32,890 --> 00:19:35,560
that we prove
universal principles. [chuckles]

416
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:36,810
Still with me?

417
00:19:36,850 --> 00:19:38,060
I'm sorry,

418
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:41,140
but I don't see how I'm supposed
to apply any of this knowledge.

419
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:44,770
Well then, let's find
a more interesting one for you.

420
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:48,190
Al-Biruni. Here's his book
on astrology.

421
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:49,740
Astrology, huh?

422
00:19:50,240 --> 00:19:51,610
[FATIMA] This should be better.

423
00:19:51,650 --> 00:19:54,160
-Now, look at this.
-[gasps]

424
00:19:54,780 --> 00:20:00,120
"The diameter of the Earth
is 2,163 and one-third farsakh,

425
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:03,170
and its circumference
is 6,800 farsakh."

426
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:06,550
Do you mean he traveled
to the ends of the Earth?

427
00:20:06,590 --> 00:20:09,050
Oh, no, that would be
quite impossible.

428
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:13,050
By forming a right triangle
using a spot on the ground,

429
00:20:13,090 --> 00:20:15,430
a mountaintop,
and the center of the Earth,

430
00:20:15,470 --> 00:20:18,260
it's then possible to determine
the Earth's radius.

431
00:20:18,310 --> 00:20:20,350
A mountaintop, huh?

432
00:20:21,980 --> 00:20:23,940
[FATIMA] There's yet
another method of calculating

433
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:26,400
the Earth's circumference
using the angle of shadows

434
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,400
on the ground.

435
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:29,150
[SITARA] Just with shadows?

436
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:31,490
[bucket clangs]

437
00:20:31,530 --> 00:20:32,610
[Sitara gasps]

438
00:20:32,990 --> 00:20:34,490
[FATIMA] All of these
were derived

439
00:20:34,530 --> 00:20:37,410
from the universal knowledge
that's found in Elements.

440
00:20:37,450 --> 00:20:39,870
Well? Is your interest piqued?

441
00:20:39,910 --> 00:20:41,160
[Sitara gasps softly]

442
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:43,080
-[gasps] It's burning!
-[Sitara yelps]

443
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:45,130
[exclaims]

444
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:48,750
[chuckles nervously]

445
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:51,960
It is one problem after another
with you lately.

446
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:54,590
I hope you'll forgive me,
Ms. Anis.

447
00:20:55,430 --> 00:20:56,970
Now listen, Sitara.

448
00:20:57,010 --> 00:21:00,020
There are slaves
who do all sorts of jobs.

449
00:21:00,060 --> 00:21:02,390
There are even those who acquire
all kinds of knowledge

450
00:21:02,430 --> 00:21:03,940
to entertain their masters.

451
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:07,810
And depending on the case,
some are promised their freedom.

452
00:21:09,020 --> 00:21:10,150
That said,

453
00:21:10,270 --> 00:21:12,360
you should never get
your hopes up too high.

454
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:16,030
Because we are in no position
to decide such things.

455
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:18,080
We're property, not people.

456
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,790
-[UNCLE] Listen, girls.
-[BOTH] Huh?

457
00:21:19,830 --> 00:21:21,450
Gather 'round, please.

458
00:21:21,830 --> 00:21:23,500
Could you also fetch Zumurrud?

459
00:21:23,540 --> 00:21:25,120
Is there something wrong?

460
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:28,840
Our militia fought,
but the nomads have won!

461
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:30,880
♪

462
00:21:33,010 --> 00:21:35,720
[SITARA (ADULT)] Heaven didn't
answer our prayers with mercy.

463
00:21:35,760 --> 00:21:37,680
They were met only with fire.

464
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:40,970
Instead of rain,
embers fell across the land,

465
00:21:41,010 --> 00:21:42,390
followed by silence...

466
00:21:43,060 --> 00:21:45,350
which took place of the flames.

467
00:22:07,250 --> 00:22:09,880
[♪ closing theme song playing]

468
00:23:37,010 --> 00:23:41,300
[SITARA (ADULT)] Next episode:
"The Roses that Bloom in Safar."

